ERIFIED intact: 20 files, 2654 insertions, dated 2026-08-08 03:42:49, author rock-solid-sites, message references gh#228.\nWorking tree carries no uncommitted investigation work (only .crosslink/.last-hydrated-ref modified and untracked .kickoff-session).\n\n== F6 Deliverable gap against the #228 brief ==\n  - report.md: ABSENT. The required deliverable does not exist in any form.\n  - Option A: logs present for a1 control, a2 selfheal-c2, a3a/a3b/a3c intermittent-flapping, plus two heal-state JSON files. Data appears collected; not synthesized.\n  - Option A2b pre-absorbed: tests/phase_a2b_preabsorbed.py present, NO corresponding log — script written, not run.\n  - Option B: tests/phase_b1_traceback.py, tests/phase_b2_poc.py, intercept_poc.py present, NO logs for b1 or b2 — scripts written, not run. B yes/no unanswered.\n  - Option C: not reached (correctly, since B is unresolved).\n\n== RECOMMENDED ORCHESTRATOR ACTIONS (I do not act; read-only) ==\n  1. Confirm whether pp3g-XBoz was ever launched. If launch failed, re-dispatch the Builder — no work is progressing on #228 right now.\n  2. Release or reassign the stale pp3g-qfOy lock on #228 before re-dispatch, else the new Builder is blocked.\n  3. Close the orphaned 44-hour session #1 so session telemetry stops accumulating against the stalled builder.\n  4. Launch auditors into their OWN worktrees. Placing the auditor in the audited worktree defeats identity separation and is itself an audit-integrity defect.\n  5. Deconflict with pp3g-cXmI, which appears to hold the same Phase-1 role.\n  6. Scope note for the re-dispatched Builder: Option A data exists and needs synthesis; A2b, B1, B2 need execution; report.md is the gating artifact.\n\nI remain pre-positioned. No files written, no fixes applied, no dispatch performed.","created_at":"2026-08-08T03:47:30.842266814Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:QnesEmvvqpIlj5hRSf8Xgt2fnafYnIlPGS2VybcvWMc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3GZ1io