{"agent_id":"pp3g-qfOy-investigation-task-decision-ready-comparison-not-a","agent_seq":11,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T03:49:31.736787169Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7ef840e7-d516-4301-b94d-f02d6d30bb55","comment_uuid":"d65060fe-496b-4a51-87a4-2f0bfa24f8cb","author":"pp3g-qfOy-investigation-task-decision-ready-comparison-not-a","content":"Completed: PHASE-1 pre-positioned auditor pass on #228 (read-only). VERDICT: divergence confirmed, escalated. Primary finding — the monitored Builder pp3g-XBoz does not exist (absent on 4 independent channels: worktree list, git authorship since 2026-08-06, crosslink comments, branch commits), re-verified 3 min later. No in-flight work existed to monitor. Secondary — this auditor was launched into the AUDITED agent's worktree, inheriting identity pp3g-qfOy, its stale #228 lock, and this very session (#1, 44h old); auditor events are mis-attributed to the builder. NOTE: ending session #1 here is simultaneously my own closeout AND the orphaned-session cleanup I recommended to the orchestrator — the two are inseparable because of that identity collision; recording this so the audit trail is not misread as an auditor performing unilateral remediation. Also confirmed: preserved evidence commit 7dd054be INTACT (20 files, 2654 insertions) on the correct branch; report.md ABSENT; Option A logs (a1/a2/a3a-c) present, Option A2b/B1/B2 scripts written but never executed, Option C not reached. Blocking orchestrator actions: confirm/redo Builder launch, release stale pp3g-qfOy lock on #228, deconflict duplicate Phase-1 role pp3g-cXmI. Phase 2 should NOT be dispatched — there is no deliverable to audit. No files written, no fixes, no dispatch.","created_at":"2026-08-08T03:49:31.729374171Z","kind":"handoff","signed_by":"SHA256:QnesEmvvqpIlj5hRSf8Xgt2fnafYnIlPGS2VybcvWMc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3GZ1ioft4osqukNxK8O3e9w3xIKe6PwYDD2kPknQ0QMAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWV