{"agent_id":"pp3g-qfOy-investigation-task-decision-ready-comparison-not-a","agent_seq":23,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T04:25:55.036906002Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"69b767bd-5895-4839-9bf9-16924d1773d2","comment_uuid":"72f9c6d9-45ba-4126-95c5-43749044a7d9","author":"pp3g-qfOy-investigation-task-decision-ready-comparison-not-a","content":"## Audit Verdict: CONDITIONAL PASS\n\nPhase-2 post-hoc audit of the C2-gap investigation (#228) — deliverable `research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/c2-gap-investigation/`, commits 7dd054be + af350f49, branch feature/pp3g-qfOy-...-not-a. Read-only. Independent: I did not read #264/#265 comments or verdicts (only their titles, unavoidably, in the #228 subissue list). Scope: the investigation only — NOT the recovery/stalled-builder incident, NOT #196/#213/#217, NOT the umbrella document.\n\n**Rationale for the verdict.** The empirical core is excellent and independently reproducible: I re-derived all 11 rows of the timing/spawn table, the traceback-origin claim, every source-read line citation, the corpus md5s, the byte-identity of the preserved logs, and the cross-document #213 baselines — and **every harness-emitted number matched exactly**. The interception claim is not merely asserted but *falsifiably demonstrated* by a stack-frame substitution visible in the committed logs. What holds it back from a clean PASS is not error in what was measured but over-reach in what was claimed: one decision-relevant property of the recommended option was inferred and presented as tested (C1), the recommended option's upgrade fragility was never assessed (C2), and the one deliverable metric the harness did NOT emit is both non-reproducible and internally inconsistent (C3). R1-R3 are the conditions; each is small and none is likely to reverse the recommendation.\n\n---\n\n### Outcome Quality — re-derivation from committed evidence\n\n**[OK] All 11 rows of the section-7 timing/spawn table reproduce exactly.** Nothing rounded, nothing rephrased:\n- A1 control 5680 ms / spawns=2 / proxy_processes=3 / persistent_proxies=2 / reconnect=True — `logs/phase-a1-control-harness.log:88,89,93`\n- A2 fresh-session 1849 / 8 / 5 ms; `spawn_increment=1 cumulative_spawns=1 persistent_proxies=1 reconnect_fired=False heal_increment=1` — `phase-a2-selfheal-c2-harness.log:30,31,39,40,48,49,54`\n- A2b pre-absorbed 1852 / 4070 / 9 ms; `backend_spawn_count=2 proxy_processes=3 persistent_proxies=2 reconnect_fired=True heal_events=1` — `phase-a2b-preabsorbed-harness.log:26,55,63,64,66`\n- A3a 1724/3730/7/7 ms; `spawns=2 persistent_proxies=2 reconnect_fired=True heal_events=1`, `after_schema=None` — `phase-a3-intermittent-harness.log:23,53,61,69,70,71`\n- A3b 1847/7/9/9 ms; `spawns=1 persistent_proxies=1 reconnect_fired=False heal_events=0 schema_failure_classified=2` — same log `:96,104,112,120,121`\n- A3c 1687/1111/1012/1020 ms; `spawns=4 persistent_proxies=1 reconnect_fired=False heal_events=0` — same log `:146,165,184,203,204`\n- B1 5561 ms — `phase-b1-traceback-harness.log:157`\n- B2 PoC 2373 ms; `backend_spawn_count=1 proxy_processes=2 persistent_proxies=1 reconnect_fired=False schema_validation_failures=1`; `B2_RESULT ... error_preserved=True interception_effective=True` — `phase-b2-poc-harness.log:70,71,74`\n\n**[OK] The traceback-origin claim is exact and triple-corroborated.** Against the live venv: `mcp/client/session.py:1110` is literally `raise RuntimeError(f'Invalid structured content returned by tool {name}: {error}') from error`; `session.py:1064` is `await self.validate_tool_result(name, result)`; `toolregistry/integrations/mcp/client.py:133` is `return await self._session.call_tool(name, arguments)` — a genuine pure pass-through (130-133 are only an assert plus the return). The frame chain appears independently in three logs: `phase-a1-control-harness.log:71-75`, `phase-b1-traceback-harness.log:41-45 / 92-96 / 140-144`, `phase-b2-poc-harness.log:53-57`. Section 5.1's claim of two identical tracebacks is confirmed.\n\n**[OK] The section-5.2 source read is exact where it matters most.** `connection.py:106` is literally `except Exception:` — the catch-all the whole argument rests on. `MCPConnectionManager` is public at `connection.py:16`; `_call_persistent` spans 97-111 as stated; `integration.py:323` is literally `connection = MCPConnectionManager(` (hardcoded, no factory/hook — confirmed); `integration.py:223` is `def from_tool_json(`; `session.py:1086` is the cache-miss test `if name not in self._tool_output_schemas:` and `session.py:1276` is `self._tool_output_schemas[tool.name] = tool.output_schema`. The mechanism narrative in section 4.2 is therefore grounded, not hand-waved.\n\n**[OK] The interception is PROVEN IN THE CALL PATH, not asserted.** This is the strongest single piece of evidence in the deliverable and deserves explicit credit: `phase-b2-poc-harness.log:51` shows the frame `intercept_poc.py, line 90, in _call_persistent` exactly where A1 (`phase-a1-control-harness.log:69`) and B1 (`phase-b1-traceback-harness.log:136`) show `connection.py, line 111, in _call_persistent`. The subclass demonstrably displaced the stock reconnect seam. That is a falsifiable structural signal, not a counter the harness could have miscounted.\n\n**[OK] Verbatim ErrorResult preservation holds character-for-character.** A1's `message_verbatim` (`:88`) and B2's (`:70`) are identical strings. Section 9's identity claim is literally true, and the contrast drawn against #217's `ToolCallResult`-with-repr degradation is corroborated by the A3b caller-visible shape at `phase-a3-intermittent-harness.log:104,120`.\n\n**[OK] Corpus integrity claims verified independently.** `backend.py` md5 `279c75202f9c2e1c2142323b020dfa6f` and `manifest.json` md5 `f8977f8a138a4a4f0861e6a0ed056f91` are byte-identical to `output-schema-drift/` — exactly the prefixes claimed in section 3.\n\n**[OK] No #213/#217 corpus modification — verified, not trusted.** `git diff --stat 77b8d2be..af350f49` = 38 files, 4278 insertions, **0 deletions**, every path under `c2-gap-investigation/`. `common_c2.py:42-45` references the #213 proxy as a read-only path (`DRIFT_PROXY = HERE.parent / 'output-schema-drift' / 'proxy.py'`) rather than copying or editing it.\n\n**[OK] The preserved-evidence claim is literally true.** All 7 files in `logs/preserved-initial-run/` are md5-identical to their 7dd054be originals (verified via `git show 7dd054be:...` vs `af350f49:...`). Section 13's word *untouched* is accurate, and the preserved set is complete (7 of 7).\n\n**[OK] Cross-document baselines check out.** Section 7's reference figures match #213 exactly: `output-schema-drift/report.md:127,350` (Test B 1810-3124 ms, n=3) and `:307,353` (C2 5871-5913 ms n=2 normal / 9008 ms load-affected, 2 spawns / 2 proxies).\n\n**[OK] Versions machine-recorded, not merely asserted.** `toolregistry=0.15.0 mcp=2.0.0 python=3.10.12 platform=linux` appears in the `phase_start` line of every one of the six harness logs.\n\n**[OK] Scope discipline respected.** stdio-only bounded explicitly (section 12); PoC-only respected (no production build, no upstream PR); Option C correctly not reached and explicitly recorded as such (section 6) rather than quietly dropped.\n\n---\n\n**[CONCERN — C1, material to the recommendation] Option B's pre-absorbed uniformity is INFERRED but presented as TESTED.**\nSection 8 states B closes the gap `in every tested session state (fresh or pre-absorbed — the interception fires regardless of what the client has absorbed)`; section 11 repeats `works uniformly whether or not the stale schema is pre-absorbed`. **No pre-absorbed test was run for Option B.** `phase-b2-poc-harness.log` contains exactly one INVOKE (`add(2,3)`, line 70) in a fresh session; `tests/run_c2.py:20-28` enumerates five phases with no B pre-absorbed analogue of A2b. This matters because the pre-absorbed axis is precisely the discriminator the recommendation turns on — A is downgraded to *partial* because of it (sections 4.5, 11). The comparison therefore rests on a measured result for A and an unmeasured inference for B. The inference is mechanically plausible (the override sits at the reconnect trigger, upstream of absorption state) and is correctly quarantined as interpretation in section 10.4 — but the phrase *every tested session state* in section 8 asserts testing that did not occur.\n\n**[CONCERN — C2] The recommended option's upgrade fragility was never assessed.**\nOption B's mechanism overrides a **private** method and **re-implements its body by copy**: `intercept_poc.py:86-103` duplicates `connection.py:101-111`, differing only by the classification branch and the dropped `logger.warning` at `connection.py:107`. Section 5.2 is honest that `_call_persistent` is private, but section 5.4 lists *the only cost* as the registration-assembly requirement, and section 11 calls B `dependency-free and patch-free` with `none of those conditions`. Overriding and duplicating a private method carries genuine upgrade fragility: if upstream alters `_call_persistent` (backoff, lock discipline, telemetry, retry count) the subclass diverges silently while still importing and passing. The brief scoped upgrade-fragility assessment to Option C only, so the report is *compliant* — but the consequence is that the winning option shipped un-assessed on the exact dimension the losing option would have been judged on. Relatedly, the summary layers compress `subclass a public class, override its private method` into `clean public seam` (sections 5.4, 8, 11), losing the caveat that section 5.2 states correctly.\n\n**[CONCERN — C3] The PoC-size deliverable is non-reproducible and internally inconsistent.**\nSection 5.3's table:\n- `Code lines (non-blank/non-comment/non-docstring) = 99` does **not** reproduce. Under the report's own stated definition, a tokenize-based count of `intercept_poc.py` gives **64**. No plausible alternative rule yields 99 (total 147; non-blank 124; non-blank and non-hash 116; post-module-docstring non-blank 88). The `147 total` figure is correct.\n- The summary sentence `The whole interception mechanism is 48 code lines (5 classifier + 20 class body incl. the 16-line override + 22 registration loop + 10 sync entry)` is internally inconsistent: **the stated addends sum to 57, not 48.**\n- Sub-unit figures do not reproduce under any one consistent rule: `_is_schema_validation_error` = 5 is correct (lines 58-62), but the `_call_persistent` override = 16 (actual 13 body-only non-comment / 20 including signature), `_register_async` = 22 (actual 16 body-only / 27 whole), `register_with_connection` = 10 (actual 11 whole / 4 body-only).\n- Section 10.4 compounds it with `a ~23-line registration assembly` where the same report's table implies 22 + 10 = 32.\nMateriality: **low for the conclusion** (48, 57 or 64 — the wrapper is small either way and the comparative verdict is unaffected) but **high for reproducibility**, because PoC size is one of the four artefacts the brief explicitly demanded and is the number an implementer would carry forward. It has already propagated: the #228 result comment (2026-08-08 03:58) says `147 lines / 48 code lines`, collapsing the file-level and mechanism-level figures, and my own Phase-2 dispatch brief repeats that collapsed form verbatim.\n\n**[CONCERN — C4] Every latency is n=1, presented as a quantified before/after.**\nSection 11's headline `2373 ms vs 5680 ms control in the same run` is one observation against one observation. This is a regression against the precedent the same table cites: #213 reported ranges with explicit n (`report.md:350` 1810-3124, n=3; `:353` 5871-5913, n=2). Mitigating: the report carries an honest host-load caveat (section 2), says *in the same run*, and the **spawn counts** — which carry most of the argument — are discrete and mechanism-determined, so n=1 is adequate for them. But no `n` is stated anywhere and no variance is reported, so the latency deltas are weaker evidence than their presentation implies.\n\n**[CONCERN — C5, minor] Asymmetric test depth favouring the rejected option.**\nOption A received 3 phases, 3 sub-scenarios, 11 measured calls. Option B received one traceback phase and a one-call PoC. B2 measures no warm-call behaviour and no other-tool-untouched property, both of which A2 measured. Recommending the less-tested option is defensible here — B's mechanism is simpler and its single result is decisive on the spawn axis — but the asymmetry is not disclosed.\n\n**[CONCERN — C6, minor] The flapping verdict rests on a single heal event, and N was never varied.**\nOf the three A3 sub-scenarios only A3a produced any heal at all (`heal_events=1`; A3b and A3c both 0). A single non-repeated heal cannot strongly exclude flapping; what A3 actually demonstrates is convergence-on-first-heal plus absence of heal-back within four calls. That is a sound and honestly-stated result, but it is narrower than *no flapping* reads. Separately, only N=1 was tested — the builder's own 2026-08-06 07:42 plan comment on #228 proposed `N=1 then a higher N to find the flapping threshold`; the threshold sweep was dropped without note. (The #228 issue text required only *verify no flapping*, so this deviates from the plan, not the brief.)\n\n**[CONCERN — C7, nit] One imprecise citation.** Section 5.2 cites `_call_per_request (113-121)`; the method spans `connection.py:113-118` (119 blank, 120 a section comment). Immaterial, and noted only because every other line citation in the report is exact.\n\n**Recommendation soundness.** Section 11 (B primary, A complementary) follows from the evidence on the axes actually measured: B reaches 1 spawn / 1 proxy / no reconnect with the error shape preserved; A reaches the same only fresh-session and needs DELTA C for intermittent drift (A3b 1 spawn vs A3c 4 spawns — verified). Section 10.5's observation that the options are complementary rather than competing (A recovers the manifest; B only removes amplification) is a genuine insight, correctly filed as interpretation. C1 and C2 qualify the recommendation; neither reverses it.\n\n---\n\n### Process Assessment\n\n- **[OK] Both commits reference the issue.** 7dd054be and af350f49 each carry `(gh#228)` in the subject line.\n- **[OK] Full workflow observed on the resumed leg.** plan (03:47) → POST-PLAN checkpoint (03:47) → MIDPOINT checkpoint (03:54) → `--kind result` (03:58) → `--kind action` (03:58) → `--kind handoff` (03:58). Matches the kickoff progress contract in cadence and in required fields.\n- **[OK] Documentation Standard YAML present and house-conformant.** `program: EDASES`, `layer: Research`, `document_type: Research Finding`, `status: Validated`, `authority: Experimental`, `canonical_repository: edases`, `depends_on: [Documentation Standard, Concept: Levels of Abstraction]`, `last_updated: 2026-08-08` — field-for-field the same shape as `output-schema-drift/report.md` and `retry-classification/report.md`, with `related_documents` correctly extended to both siblings plus the parent report.\n- **[OK] Observation/finding separation is declared AND honoured.** Declared at report.md:55-57; every phase tabulates observations with an Evidence column carrying the literal log token; interpretation is quarantined in section 10, explicitly titled *Findings (interpretation, distinct from observations)*. This is the AGENTS.md evidence discipline actually implemented, not just cited.\n- **[OK] Exact versions recorded in the report AND machine-emitted per phase** (section 2 plus every `phase_start` line) — belt and braces.\n- **[OK] Deliverable complete against the brief.** A before/after cost numbers and flapping check present; B yes/no, traceback and PoC size present (size figures defective per C3, but present); C correctly not reached and explicitly recorded; one-paragraph recommendation present (section 11); logs, PoC scripts and a reproduce command all present (section 3).\n- **[OK — commendable] Evidence-preservation discipline is exemplary.** Rather than overwrite the stalled run's logs, the resumed work copied all 7 into `logs/preserved-initial-run/` (md5-verified identical), labelled every quoted number *fresh* vs *preserved*, and disclosed the host-load confound with concrete `init_ms` figures (section 2). This is the right instinct and I want it on the record as a positive, not merely as an absence of fault.\n- **[CONCERN — minor] Placeholder left in the durable reasoning trail.** The first plan comment on #228 (2026-08-06 07:27) reads `Plan: <placeholder test>` and was never retracted or annotated. AGENTS.md names reasoning as the primary object of interest; placeholder artefacts sitting permanently above the real plan dilute exactly that.\n- **[CONCERN — minor] The result comment degraded a report figure.** The 03:58 `--kind result` on #228 states `intercept_poc.py 147 lines / 48 code lines`, which is not what the report says (147 total / 99 claimed file code lines / 48 claimed mechanism lines). The summary layer lost the distinction, and the lossy form is what propagated downstream.\n- **[OBSERVATION, out of scope] #228's comment trail interleaves the investigation with the Phase-1 recovery auditor's F1-F7 findings.** I have not audited those, per scope. Noting only that the interleaving makes #228 hard to read as a single investigation record.\n\n---\n\n### Architectural Assessment\n\n- **[OK] Layer discipline correct.** The deliverable lives in `research/`, is typed `layer: Research` / `document_type: Research Finding` / `authority: Experimental`, and confines itself to evidence plus clearly-marked interpretation. Section 11 recommends a direction without promoting itself to methodology; no ASES-layer or Execution-Engine artefact was created or amended. Implementation-level detail (subclass seams, line numbers) appears as *observed evidence about a third-party library* — research observing implementation, which is the legitimate direction of dependency, not research depending on implementation.\n- **[OK] Identifier-first framing respected.** Section 1 positions the work precisely as the C2 residue of #213's Test C2 that #217 explicitly did not cover, names the mechanism (`connection.py:106`), and links #213, #217 and the parent umbrella in `related_documents`. It extends the line rather than re-litigating it.\n- **[OK] Corpus isolation is architecturally clean and independently verified.** Byte-identical inputs (md5-checked by the builder, re-checked by me), a read-only path reference to the #213 proxy (`common_c2.py:42-45`), zero deletions across the entire diff, and all proxy deltas documented as DELTA A/B/C in `proxy_self_heal.py`'s docstring. This makes the C2 numbers genuinely comparable to #213/#217 rather than merely similar — which is what allows section 7's cross-document baseline row to be meaningful.\n- **[OK] stdio-only scope respected and explicitly bounded** (section 12), matching #196/#213/#217. No transport generalisation attempted anywhere.\n- **[CONCERN] Tooling-independence boundary is thinned at the summary layer.** AGENTS.md requires methodology to stay independent of implementation tooling. Section 11's recommendation is a specific coupling to a specific *private* method of a specific version of a specific library. That is entirely appropriate as research evidence, and the report keeps it in the research layer — but because the document is titled *decision-ready* and names a *primary* option, it sits one hop from being read as direction. Critically, the version-boundedness (`toolregistry 0.15.0` / `mcp 2.0.0`) is recorded in section 2 but absent from the title, section 8 and section 11 — the three places a reader will quote. C2 is the concrete face of this.\n\n---\n\n### Systemic Risks Identified\n\n- **S1 — Agent-computed metrics propagate upward unverified, while harness-emitted metrics do not fail.** Impact: the corpus accumulates unfalsifiable numbers. The contrast inside this one deliverable is sharp and diagnostic — every harness-emitted figure (`A1_RESULT`, `B2_SPAWN_COUNTS`, `delta_ms`, `A3_METRICS`) reproduced exactly; every agent-computed line count did not. Traced propagation: report section 5.3 (99/48, non-reproducible and inconsistent) → #228 result comment 03:58 (conflated to `147 lines / 48 code lines`) → my Phase-2 dispatch brief (verbatim). Three hops, no verification, degraded at hop two. Mitigation: require derived metrics to be emitted by a committed script (e.g. `tests/measure_poc_size.py` writing to a log) so they fall under the same re-derivation discipline as timings.\n- **S2 — *Decision-ready* outruns test coverage on the deciding axis.** Impact: comparisons read as symmetric when they are not, and downstream readers inherit an inference as a measurement (C1). Mitigation: require every comparison document to carry an option-by-condition coverage matrix with explicit `not tested` cells, so an absent cell is visible rather than smoothed over by prose.\n- **S3 — Recommended options escape the scrutiny applied to rejected ones.** The brief attached upgrade-fragility assessment to Option C alone — the option pre-judged as ugly. B won and therefore shipped un-assessed on the very dimension C would have been judged on, despite B also depending on a private, version-bound internal. Impact: selection criteria vary by option, systematically favouring whichever option the brief pre-framed as clean. Mitigation: make fragility assessment a property of the *recommended* option, not of a pre-designated one.\n- **S4 — Statistical rigour is drifting down across the identifier-first line.** #213 reported n=2/n=3 ranges; #228 reports n=1 points with no `n` stated, while quoting #213's ranges in the same table (section 7). Impact: the umbrella will silently mix n=3 ranges with n=1 points. Mitigation: state `n` on every latency in this line, or mark single-shot values as such.\n- **S5 — Two reusable constraints are trapped in a phase report.** (a) The C2 exception is SDK-origin at `mcp/client/session.py:1110` and ToolRegistry 0.15.0 has *no* failure-class distinction anywhere in its MCP integration (`connection.py:106` catches bare `Exception`). (b) `register_from_mcp` hardcodes `MCPConnectionManager` at `integration.py:323`, so *any* connection-layer customisation in this stack requires manual registration assembly. Both are load-bearing for every future option in the identifier-first line, not just C2. Impact: guaranteed rediscovery cost. Mitigation: promote both into the umbrella document and/or a Crosslink knowledge page keyed to the exact versions, under epic #212.\n- **S6 — Version-bound findings carry no expiry marker.** Every Option B conclusion is valid only for `toolregistry==0.15.0` + `mcp==2.0.0` and depends on private internals with no compatibility guarantee, yet sections 8 and 11 state their conclusions unconditionally. Impact: after the next upgrade the report reads as current while potentially being void, with no signal to re-run. Mitigation: add version-validity lines to the conclusion sections and file a re-validation trigger against #212.\n\n---\n\n### Recommendations\n\n- **R1 — Run a B2b pre-absorbed phase; substantiate or retract the uniformity claim. [HIGH]** Rationale: this is the single load-bearing untested claim in the recommendation (C1), it sits on the axis that decides A vs B, and the A2b harness pattern already exists to copy — roughly 15 minutes of work to close the gap or correct sections 8 and 11.\n- **R2 — Correct the section 5.3 PoC-size table and the `48 (5+20+22+10)` sentence; state the counting rule and emit the counts from a committed script; reconcile section 10.4's `~23-line`. [HIGH]** Rationale: PoC size is a named deliverable, the current figures are non-reproducible and internally self-contradictory, and the error has already propagated two hops (C3, S1).\n- **R3 — Add an upgrade-fragility paragraph for Option B and qualify section 11's `dependency-free and patch-free`. [HIGH]** Rationale: the recommended option is currently the only one whose fragility was never assessed; cite the concrete coupling (`intercept_poc.py:86-103` duplicating `connection.py:101-111`, including the dropped `logger.warning`) so the risk is specific rather than abstract (C2, S3).\n- **R4 — State `n` for every latency, or mark section 7 values as single-shot. [MEDIUM]** Rationale: aligns with the #213 precedent the same table cites and prevents the umbrella from mixing n=3 ranges with n=1 points (C4, S4).\n- **R5 — Add a Limitations section recording what was NOT tested. [MEDIUM]** Specifically: no B pre-absorbed run, no B warm-call or other-tool measurement, N never varied above 1, single host, stdio only. Rationale: the report's honesty is high throughout *except* that absences are invisible; a limitations block converts silent gaps into declared scope (C1, C5, C6).\n- **R6 — Promote the two reusable constraints (S5a, S5b) into the umbrella document and/or a versioned Crosslink knowledge page. [MEDIUM]** Rationale: they constrain every future option in the identifier-first line; leaving them in a phase report guarantees rediscovery under epic #212.\n- **R7 — Add version-validity statements to sections 8 and 11 and file a re-validation trigger on #212 for toolregistry/mcp upgrades. [LOW]** Rationale: the conclusions are version-bound but currently read as unconditional (S6).\n- **R8 — Process hygiene. [LOW]** Retract or annotate the `Plan: <placeholder test>` comment on #228; correct the result comment's `147 lines / 48 code lines` conflation; fix section 5.2's `_call_per_request (113-121)` to `(113-118)`. Rationale: the reasoning trail is the project's primary artefact, and placeholders plus lossy summaries degrade it.\n\n---\n\n**Summary.** Strong, disciplined, independently reproducible empirical work with exemplary evidence preservation and clean layer/scope containment. The measured results are trustworthy — I checked them and they hold. The gap is between what was measured and what was claimed, concentrated in three specific, cheaply-fixable places (R1, R2, R3). CONDITIONAL PASS on those three.","created_at":"2026-08-08T04:25:55.023180146Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:QnesEmvvqpIlj5hRSf8Xgt2fnafYnIlPGS2VybcvWMc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3GZ1ioft4osqukNxK8O3e9w3xIKe6PwYDD2kPknQ0QMAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAl8mw8p3Yo3ku+0KOIwOVDVUDaezA5Cno8MK5Snp+XNNFLJrNifuzI5l9+zrhJOYwM231+N0dmqsqBVbH/i2dAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:QnesEmvvqpIlj5hRSf8Xgt2fnafYnIlPGS2VybcvWMc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3GZ1ioft4osqukNxK8O3e9w3xIKe6PwYDD2kPknQ0QMAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCBPGVMGrCPsXFfTE5q8Ia7heJF6ytIWHe8xG4S1Sr6I6StcQsbcKPeCLUABpCfckKHvBGJTLm/DuHHtGJ5DPQM="}
