{"agent_id":"pp3g-qfOy-investigation-task-decision-ready-comparison-not-a","agent_seq":32,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T05:37:37.594182332Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5b48669e-0dbc-4b1b-a62c-3a5dc82c7f8c","comment_uuid":"8041bd98-faa0-4ed5-b594-2ff335b1010d","author":"pp3g-qfOy-investigation-task-decision-ready-comparison-not-a","content":"## Audit Verdict: CONDITIONAL PASS\n\nAuditor: big-pickle (backfill for the north-mini-code slot that failed at launch; see the 04:23 observation on this issue). Independent — sibling Phase-2 audits #263/#264 not read. Scope: C2-gap investigation (#228), deliverable research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/c2-gap-investigation/, commits 7dd054be + af350f49, HEAD = af350f49. Recovery/stalled-builder incident explicitly excluded.\n\n### Outcome Quality — evidence re-derivation\n\nEvery checkable number in report.md re-derives exactly from the committed logs. Verified one-by-one against logs/:\n\n- A1 control 2 spawns / 2 persistent proxies (3 proxy pids) / reconnect YES / 5680 ms: phase-a1-control-harness.log INVOKE delta_ms=5680; A1_SPAWN_COUNTS backend_spawn_count=2 proxy_processes=3 persistent_proxies=2 reconnect_fired=True; proxy_pids=[682161,682172,682223] = registration temp + 2 persistent.\n- A2 self-heal fresh: call 1 SUCCESS 1849 ms at 1 spawn / 1 persistent proxy / no reconnect (INVOKE delta_ms=1849 ok=True result='5.0'; A2_CALL_METRICS spawn_increment=1 cumulative_spawns=1 persistent_proxies=1 reconnect_fired=False); warm calls 8 ms and 5 ms with spawn_increment=0; heal event with before/after schema (A2_HEAL_EVENT; self_heal ... after_schema={'properties': {'result': ...}}); other tool multiply untouched (A2_SERVED ... 'multiply': None).\n- A2b pre-absorbed boundary: multiply 1852 ms; first drifted add 4070 ms SUCCESS-after-retry; A2B_SPAWN_COUNTS backend_spawn_count=2 persistent_proxies=2 reconnect_fired=True heal_events=1; repeat add 9 ms warm; heal_state_loaded by the respawned proxy confirmed (the persisted-heal mechanism is real, not asserted).\n- A3 flapping check: A3_METRICS a3a spawns=2 persistent_proxies=2 reconnect_fired=True heal_events=1 (heal converges to None, no heal-back); a3b spawns=1 persistent_proxies=1 reconnect_fired=False schema_failure_classified=2; a3c spawns=4 persistent_proxies=1 reconnect_fired=False (respawn chain be-1→be-4 visible). Latencies 1724/3730/7/7, 1847/7/9/9, 1687/1111/1012/1020 all match §7.\n- B1 traceback: SDK-origin claim confirmed against the installed source — mcp/client/session.py:1110 raises the RuntimeError (verified by direct read), called from session.py:1064; toolregistry client.py:133 is a pure pass-through (read line 133); connection.py:106 is the catch-all reconnect in _call_persistent (read lines 97-111). Two identical tracebacks captured (attempt + retry) in phase-b1-traceback-harness.log. INVOKE delta_ms=5561; spawns=2 reconnect=True.\n- B2 PoC: B2_SPAWN_COUNTS backend_spawn_count=1 proxy_processes=2 persistent_proxies=1 reconnect_fired=False schema_validation_failures=1; INVOKE delta_ms=2373 ok=False outcome_type=ErrorResult with message_verbatim identical to A1's control text (verified byte-for-byte in the two harness logs); B2_RESULT error_preserved=True. Traceback in the B2 log shows the interception active (intercept_poc.py line 90 in _call_persistent).\n- Source-read claims all verified against /tmp/toolregistry-venv (still present): MCPConnectionManager public at connection.py:16; register_mcp_tools_async hardcodes MCPConnectionManager at integration.py:323 with no injection point (lines 296-352); MCPTool.from_tool_json public classmethod at integration.py:223; _absorb_tool_listing at session.py:1247 with the schema-store write at 1276 (report's 1273-1276 citation is the correct region).\n- Versions verified live: mcp-2.0.0.dist-info and toolregistry-0.15.0.dist-info present in the venv.\n- Corpus identity verified: backend.py md5 279c75202f9c2e1c2142323b020dfa6f and manifest.json md5 f8977f8a138a4a4f0861e6a0ed056f91 match the report's claimed prefixes.\n- §7 baseline cross-refs verified against the #213 corpus: 1810-3124 ms success, 5871-5913 ms normal / 9008 ms load-affected C2 failure, 2 spawns/2 proxies (output-schema-drift/report.md:127,307,350-353).\n- Recommendation (§11) follows from the evidence: B is smaller/uniform/shape-preserving; A is fresh-session-conditional and delta-dependent. No over-claiming of A (§4.5/§8 qualify fresh vs pre-absorbed correctly); C correctly marked NOT REACHED (§6); stdio-only scope respected (§12, transport dicts are command/args/env); PoC-only respected; no #213/#217 corpus modification (both commits touch only c2-gap-investigation/; DRIFT_PROXY is a read-only reference, common_c2.py:22-25; originals preserved untouched in logs/preserved-initial-run/).\n\n[CONCERN] PoC-size arithmetic does not reconcile (report.md §5.3). The enumerated components 5 classifier + 20 class body + 22 registration + 10 sync entry sum to 57, not the headline 48; the per-component counts are each individually correct against intercept_poc.py (verified: 147 total via wc -l; override = 16 lines 79-103 minus docstring/comments; class body = 65+75-77+override = 20; _register_async = 6 signature + 16 body = 22; sync entry = 6 signature + 4 body = 10), so 48 is unexplained. Additionally the table's 'Code lines (non-blank/non-comment/non-docstring) = 99' is mislabeled: 147 − 41 module docstring − 7 comment lines = 99 only if 15 blank lines, the shebang, and 19 nested-docstring lines are counted as code. Strict code is 64 lines; the mechanism proper (excluding 6 imports + 1 constant) is 57 — which equals the component sum. The '48' headline is propagated to §8, §11 and the #228 result comment; the kickoff brief repeated it. Severity low (functional result unaffected) but a decision-ready deliverable should have reconcilable size claims.\n\n[CONCERN] 'Tested' vs 'argued from mechanism' imprecision (§8). The report states B works 'in every tested session state (fresh or pre-absorbed)'; only fresh-session B2 was executed (phase-b2-poc-harness.log). The pre-absorbed uniform claim is a sound inference (the interception fires at the raise site inside _call_persistent regardless of client cache state — A2b shows the same RuntimeError fires pre-absorbed) but it was not directly tested. Minor language overreach in an otherwise carefully observation/finding-separated report.\n\n### Process Assessment\n\n- [OK] Workflow followed on the completed run: resume plan (03:47) → [PROGRESS] post-plan (03:47) → [PROGRESS] midpoint after all phases re-run (03:54) → result (03:58) → handoff with notes (03:58). Both commits reference gh#228 in the message.\n- [OK] Documentation Standard YAML conformant: program EDASES, layer Research, document_type Research Finding (both permitted values per docs/standards/Documentation Standard.md:112,124,138), plus status/authority/canonical_repository/depends_on/related_documents/implements/implemented_by/supersedes/superseded_by/last_updated; consistent with sibling reports (retry-classification/report.md:1-20, output-schema-drift/report.md:1-20).\n- [OK] Observations vs findings separated: §1 declares the distinction, observation tables carry file/line evidence, §10 is labelled interpretation.\n- [OK] Exact versions recorded (§2) and re-confirmed live.\n- [OK] Deliverable complete vs the brief: report present; A before/after + flapping check; B yes/no + traceback + PoC size; C explicitly not reached; one-paragraph recommendation; logs/ with harness+proxy per phase; reproduce commands included.\n- [OK] Original evidence preserved: the load-affected initial run is untouched under logs/preserved-initial-run/ (same sizes as in 7dd054be) while fresh-run logs replaced the top-level files; af350f49 diff shows the move.\n- [INFO] The 07:27 '<placeholder test>' plan comment on #228 is a kickoff-template artifact, not builder error; the real plan replaced it at 07:42.\n\n### Systemic Risks Identified\n\n1. Size-reporting arithmetic not validated — Impact: a required deliverable element ('PoC size') carries an unreconciled headline; in a decision-ready comparison, downstream readers (epic #212, umbrella) can propagate the wrong number. Mitigation: add a mechanical check (components sum to headline) to the investigation-report checklist. Confidence: observed once; low frequency.\n2. 'Tested' language drift — Impact: an inference can be cited as evidence by downstream consumers. Mitigation: report-level convention requiring 'tested' to be reserved for directly measured states (cf. AGENTS.md evidence-vs-inference discipline).\n3. .kickoff-status false-RUNNING for read-only roles — Impact: every auditor/reviewer leaves a permanently RUNNING flag (Phase-1 auditor F7 documented this; this audit will reproduce it). Mitigation: already recommended to orchestrator (remove write-DONE step from read-only templates; treat result comment + session end as completion).\n4. Audit-slot availability under free-tier saturation — Impact: #265 was marked unavailable 04:23Z (two free-model launch failures); this audit proceeded only via paid-model backfill. Mitigation: prefer paid models for critical gates (matches existing model-routing matrix guidance).\n\n### Recommendations\n\n- R1 (HIGH — the condition): Reconcile §5.3 PoC-size counts with a stated counting method; the components sum to 57 (strict code) and the table's 99 is mislabeled — correct both and re-verify any downstream '48' citation (report §8/§11, #228 result comment, umbrella/epic notes). One-file edit, 10 minutes.\n- R2 (MEDIUM): Feed the verified durable facts into epic #212 / the identifier-first umbrella: SDK-origin raise at session.py:1110, ToolRegistry 0.15.0 has no failure-class distinction, clean seam = MCPConnectionManager._call_persistent subclass + public registration assembly, register_from_mcp hardcodes the manager (integration.py:323). These are the architecture inputs the investigation was commissioned to produce.\n- R3 (LOW): Optionally add a B2-preabsorbed run (~5 min, same harness) so §8's uniformity claim becomes tested rather than inferred; or relabel it 'argued from mechanism'.\n- R4 (MEDIUM): Fix the kickoff template — remove the placeholder '<placeholder test>' plan comment and the write-DONE-to-.kickoff-status step for read-only roles.\n- R5 (LOW): Adopt a 'tested vs inferred' label convention across research reports in this line (#196/#213/#217/#228).\n\n### Completion note\n\nRead-only role: .kickoff-status cannot be written (edit deny). The result comment + session end are the authoritative completion state; .kickoff-status will read RUNNING permanently for this worktree (systemic risk 3).","created_at":"2026-08-08T05:37:37.584512453Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:QnesEmvvqpIlj5hRSf8Xgt2fnafYnIlPGS2VybcvWMc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3GZ1ioft4osqukNxK8O3e9w3xIKe6PwYDD2kPknQ0QMAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAPr7n5iXjLa4HLBjLGqjSUJW6li4HLIKzGil7CHHcQzRAqd0Z8P0lG42OFPsb7smXmNuZ1dYRQoS4irM0RQGIDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:QnesEmvvqpIlj5hRSf8Xgt2fnafYnIlPGS2VybcvWMc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3GZ1ioft4osqukNxK8O3e9w3xIKe6PwYDD2kPknQ0QMAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJJXj0Kna3Ae28HsCtl1J9mU5JYS9lE+l5drlOl1b9phAlQGnsljqiOsRZtKDjFhMapfyw7iW3bzAH1jCZUY/gg="}
